  "learnItFirst": "**A pictograph** uses pictures to show information. The **KEY** tells you what each picture is worth.\n\n```\nKEY: 🍎 = 1 student\n\nApple:   🍎🍎🍎🍎        → 4 students like apple\nGrapes:  🍎🍎🍎🍎🍎      → 5 students like grapes\n```\n\n**When 1 icon = more than 1 unit:**\n```\nKEY: 📕 = 2 books\n\nRiya:  📕📕📕   → 3 icons × 2 books = 6 books\n```\n\n**Half an icon** means half the value:\n```\nKEY: 📕 = 2 books\nHalf a 📕 = 1 book (half of 2)\n```\n\n### 🧠 How to Solve — 3 Easy Steps\n1. **Read the key first** — always check what 1 icon is worth before answering anything.\n2. **Count the icons** for each category.\n3. **Multiply** (icons × key value) to get the real total, then add/subtract/compare as needed.\n\n---",
